 "text": "Pryderi, also named Gwri, is a Welsh hero in the first branch of the Welsh tales called the Mabinogion. He was born to the magical woman Rhiannon and the human prince Pwyll. Their courtship was strange, and Rhiannon may have been a goddess. On the night of the feast of Beltane the boy vanished and blood showed on his mother's mouth, so Rhiannon was accused of killing and eating her son. The boy was not e. A creature carried him away and set him on a distant farm. The farmer Teyrnon, whose colt was saved from a monster on that same night, adopted the boy and raised him under the name Gwri. When Gwri learned the truth, he went to claim his right. He freed Rhiannon from her load, and she named him Pryderi, which means care, for all that she had suffered.",
 "okr": {
  "objective": "Describe the birth, rescue, and naming of the Welsh main hero Pryderi.",
